WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:08.980
A well-organised email makes you look professional
and is much easier for your reader to understand.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.830
Here are some tips to help you write clear,
organised messages.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:19.470
It's best to start your email with the reason
you are writing it.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:26.240
This isn’t as important in informal emails,
but in a business email you shouldn’t waste

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.010
time - get to the point!

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:37.079
A good sentence to begin with is ‘I am writing
to…’followed by a suitable verb.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:43.260
For example, ‘I am writing to ask for more
information about your event’, or ‘I am

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.600
writing to inform you of my new postal address’.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.170
Emails are easiest to read if they are broken
up into paragraphs.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.780
Email paragraphs are usually shorter than
in normal writing, with most being two or

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.989
three sentences long.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.980
This isn’t a firm rule, but if in doubt,
keep them short.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.860
You should begin a new paragraph each time
you change topic, and each paragraph should

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.800
start on a new line.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.290
For example: If you are emailing a colleague
to discuss two issues and plan a meeting,

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.250
you should write these in three separate paragraphs.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:32.360
Many people read emails on their phones, and
long email paragraphs can be frustrating to

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.450
read, especially on a small screen.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:43.310
Last, to make your emails as clear as possible,
you still need to proofread an email before

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:48.000
you send it to avoid any grammar or spelling
errors.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.090
Most email services include a spellchecker
feature to help you do this.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.200
You could also get a friend or co-worker to
check through your message.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:04.460
Subscribe to our channel for more videos on
how to improve your English language skills.

